o the number of days. It now multiplies them.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` returned `n + 1` events because of an off-by-one in the slice. It now returns the last `n`.\n- **`factory.py`:** `sample_books` was missing the third title, so I added `Emma` by Austen (1815, 1 copy). The author, year and copy count are my choice, since the tests only check the title.\n\u001b[0m\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:44:52 +1ms service=session session=ses_e9b12002bffefphMbcewTtcAv6 type=finish-step part\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:44:52 +0ms service=bus type=message.part.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:44:52 +1ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:44:52 +0ms service=session session=ses_e9b12002bffefphMbcewTtcAv6 type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:44:52 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:44:52 +5ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-22T18:44:52 +0ms service=session session=ses_e9b12002bffefphMbcewTtcAv6 sessionID=ses_e9b12002bffefphMbcewTtcAv6 unlocking\n`python3 -m unittest` now passes: 16 tests, all OK. I didn't modify any tests.\n\nThe fixes in `catalog/`:\n- **`search.py`:** it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist. It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n- **`books.py`:** `parse_book` left the year as a string. It now converts it to an int.\n- **`members.py`:** `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the comment and tests say five. It's now 5.\n- **`fees.py`:** `late_fee` added the daily fee to the number of days. It now multiplies them.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` returned `n + 1` events because of an off-by-one in the slice. It now returns the last `n`.\n- **`factory.py`:** `sample_books` was missing the third title, so I added `Emma` by Austen (1815, 1 copy). The author, year and copy count are my choice, since the tests only check the title.INFO  2026-10-22T18:44:52 +2ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_request